From d3c1b170721f73607d01cdda8f5b25835fa976f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 07:56:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cdng: direct I/O for uncompressed DNGs, IFD-first layout,
 page-aligned raw copies

Buffered writes with posix_fadvise(DONTNEED) made every recorded DNG a
16.6 MB page-cache writeback burst, the load that drops Clear HDR frames
at the CFE on this Pi (an idle buffered dd reproduces it, dd oflag=direct
does not). Uncompressed cDNG files are now written with O_DIRECT: the TIFF
header and IFD fill the first page(s), StripOffsets points at the next
page boundary, the raw copy is page aligned so 16-bit frames are written
straight from it, and the zero-padded last page is cut with ftruncate.
APERTAR_CDNG_DIRECT_IO=0 restores buffered writes; a filesystem that
refuses O_DIRECT (EINVAL) falls back by itself. Lossless cDNG, MLV and
stills are unchanged. Not compiled here: build on the Pi.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T93jucKMhWYnQM1yyFVkbH
